## Why This Is Asked
This new angle tests per-key dedupe across topics, TTL-based eviction, and correct offset commits under out-of-order delivery, a common real-world challenge not covered by the existing questions.

## Key Concepts
- Per-key deduplication
- TTL-based in-memory cache
- Cross-topic idempotence
- Out-of-order handling
- Offset commit semantics

## Code Example
```javascript
class DedupeSink {
  constructor(ttlMs=60000) {
    this.cache=new Map();
    this.ttl=ttlMs;
    this.startCleaner();
  }
  onMessage(ctx, msg) {
    const k=msg.key; const id=msg.id;
    const last=this.cache.get(k);
    if(last != null && id<=last) return false;
    this.cache.set(k,id);
    return true;
  }
  commitOffsets() { /* commit logic */ }
  dedupeStore() { return this.cache; }
  startCleaner(){ setInterval(()=>{ /* evict old entries */ }, this.ttl); }
}
```

