Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical deletion workflows in multi-tenant KCNA, balancing legal rights, data minimization, and system integrity. It requires concrete mappings, key management, tombstone strategies, and test plans that prove irreversibility while keeping performance acceptable.

Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped data maps and identifiers
- Per-tenant key rotation and re-encryption
- Tombstones, garbage collection, and index scrubbing
- Auditing, proofs, and compliance testing
- Backups, restores, and consistency guarantees

Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton
function eraseTenantData(tenantId) {
  revokeAccess(tenantId);
  rotateKeys(tenantId);
  scrubIngest(tenantId);
  scrubEnrichment(tenantId);
  scrubAnalytics(tenantId);
  publishTombstones(tenantId);
}
```

Follow-up Questions

